{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLrme41n8fQyZThdfLu2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: all four methods now raise `TypeError: Must pass only LinearEntity objects` when either argument isn't a line, instead of crashing with an `AttributeError`.\n\nThe cause was a wrong condition in the type check. In `sympy/geometry/line.py` it read `not isinstance(l1, LinearEntity) and not isinstance(l2, LinearEntity)`, so it only raised when *both* arguments were invalid. With one valid line and one `Point`, the check passed and the code failed later on `.direction`. I changed `and` to `or` in `angle_between`, `smallest_angle_between`, `is_parallel` and `is_perpendicular`, which is a 4-line diff.\n\nI ran the example from the issue against all four methods and each now raises the `TypeError`. The existing tests in `sympy/geometry/tests/test_line.py` all pass (36 tests)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":592,"cache_read_input_tokens":18836,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":592},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7f90f1ee-828f-494c-bacc-5a91e41902dc","uuid":"7e24bdc0-da42-4aea-9b3f-cbd8fb88eb43","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:08:21.407Z","request_id":"req_011ChLrmdjfQAUW1bRZ5KKMp"}
